      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If it is, I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
